### Explanation
- If the antecedent is false the property passes vacuously (watch for vacuity in coverage).
- Both are only allowed in properties, not in sequences.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- A common off-by-one bug is writing `|->` when the design responds one cycle later.

### Follow-ups
- *How to check vacuity?* Add `cover property (req)` or use tool vacuity reports.

**Key idea:** `$past(sig, N)` returns the sampled value N clock ticks ago (default 1); `$rose(sig)` is true when the LSB sampled value went 0->1 since the previous tick; `$fell(sig)` when it went 1->0. `$stable` and `$changed` complete the set.

```systemverilog
// data must be stable while valid && !ready (backpressure)
a_hold: assert property (@(posedge clk) disable iff (!rst_n)
  $past(valid && !ready) |-> $stable(data) && valid);

// a rising start must be followed by busy next cycle
a_busy: assert property (@(posedge clk) $rose(start) |=> busy);

// counter increments by 1 when en
a_inc: assert property (@(posedge clk) en |=> cnt == $past(cnt) + 1'b1);
```

```wavedrom
{"signal": [{"name": "clk", "wave": "p......"}, {"name": "start", "wave": "0.1..0."}, {"name": "$rose(start)", "wave": "0.10..."}, {"name": "$fell(start)", "wave": "0....10"}], "head": {"text": "sampled-value functions compare the current and previous sampled value"}}
```

### Explanation
- Values are from the Preponed region, so `$rose` is true at the first clock edge where the sampled value is 1 and the previous was 0.
- `$past(x, 2, en)` uses a gating expression: only ticks where `en` was true count.

### Corner cases & pitfalls
- At the first clock tick, `$past` returns the initial value (often X/0) -> guard with reset or `disable iff`.

### Follow-ups
- *`$rose` on a vector?* Only the LSB is considered; use `$changed` for vectors.

**Key idea:** A skid buffer registers `ready` toward the upstream (breaking the combinational ready path) and adds one spare register to catch the item that was sent in the cycle when downstream ready dropped. It keeps full throughput with registered ready.

```systemverilog
module skid_buffer #(parameter int W = 32) (
  input  logic clk, rst_n,
  input  logic         s_valid, output logic s_ready, input  logic [W-1:0] s_data,
  output logic         m_valid, input  logic m_ready, output logic [W-1:0] m_data);
  logic         skid_valid;
  logic [W-1:0] skid_data;

  // upstream ready is a register: high when the skid slot is empty
  always_ff @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n)
    if (!rst_n) begin
      skid_valid <= 1'b0; m_valid <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
      if (s_ready) begin                      // can accept from upstream
        if (m_valid && !m_ready) begin        // output stalled -> park in skid
          skid_valid <= s_valid;
          skid_data  <= s_data;
        end else begin                        // output free -> pass through
          m_valid <= s_valid;
          m_data  <= s_data;
        end
      end else if (m_ready) begin             // drain skid into output
        m_valid    <= 1'b1;
        m_data     <= skid_data;
        skid_valid <= 1'b0;
      end
    end
  assign s_ready = !skid_valid;
endmodule
```

